/-!
# Ideals of multivariate polynomial rings

Let `J` be the ideal of `R[X_i : i ∈ σ]` generated by the variables. It is the kernel of the
constant coefficient, and its powers are characterised by total degree.

The `k`-th power `J ^ k` consists of the polynomials all of whose monomials have total degree at
least `k` (`MvPolynomial.mem_pow_idealOfVars_iff`). This file records that multiplying an element of
`J ^ k` by any `q` only involves the constant coefficient of `q` in total degrees at most `k`.
This is how a linear map between free modules over `R[X_i : i ∈ σ]` acts, in the lowest degree
of the `J`-adic filtration, through its reduction modulo the variables. It also records that `J`
is maximal over a field, and that over a nontrivial base `J` is finitely generated if and only if
`σ` is finite, so `R[X_i : i ∈ σ]` is not noetherian when `σ` is infinite.

For arbitrary ideals given by generating sets, adjoining one auxiliary variable reduces their
intersection to contraction: multiply the first family by `X none` and the second by
`1 - X none`, then contract along `rename some`. Similarly, the saturation of an ideal `I` by a
polynomial `f`, the set of `g` with `f ^ n * g ∈ I` for some `n`, is the contraction along
`rename some` of `I + (f X_none - 1)`; it is also the contraction of `I` from the localization
away from `f`. Likewise, the relations of a polynomial parametrization are the contraction of
its graph equations `Y i - f i`. These formulas need no monomial order.

## Main results

* `MvPolynomial.ker_constantCoeff`: the kernel of the constant coefficient is the ideal generated
  by the variables.
* `MvPolynomial.X_mem_ideal_span_X_image_iff`: over a nontrivial base, `X i` lies in the ideal
  generated by `X '' s` if and only if `i ∈ s`.
* `MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.apply_lt_of_mem_sq_idealOfVars`: for positive weights, any
  variable occurring in a weight-`m` polynomial in the square of the ideal of variables has weight
  strictly below `m`.
* `MvPolynomial.map_aeval_idealOfVars`, `MvPolynomial.map_eval₂Hom_idealOfVars`: evaluating the
  ideal of the variables gives the ideal spanned by their values.
* `MvPolynomial.pow_idealOfVars_le_comap_map`: a change of coefficients maps the `k`-th power of
  the ideal of the variables into the `k`-th power of the ideal of the variables.
* `MvPolynomial.comap_map_quotient_mk_span_X_image`: the preimage of the ideal generated by
  `X '' s` under coefficient reduction modulo `I` is `I.map C ⊔ Ideal.span (X '' s)`.
* `MvPolynomial.isMaximal_idealOfVars`: over a field, the ideal of the variables is maximal.
* `MvPolynomial.not_fg_idealOfVars`, `MvPolynomial.fg_idealOfVars_iff`, and
  `MvPolynomial.not_isNoetherianRing`: over a nontrivial commutative semiring, the ideal of
  variables is finitely generated if and only if the index type is finite, so `MvPolynomial σ R`
  is not noetherian when `σ` is infinite.
* `MvPolynomial.coeff_mul_of_mem_pow_idealOfVars`: for `p ∈ J ^ k` and a monomial `e` of total
  degree at most `k`, the coefficient of `e` in `p * q` is the coefficient of `e` in `p` times the
  constant coefficient of `q`.
* `MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_of_sub_monomial_mem_pow_idealOfVars`: polynomials whose lowest
  terms are nonzero multiples of pairwise distinct monomials are linearly independent.
* `MvPolynomial.ker_killCompl` and `MvPolynomial.quotientSpanXImageEquiv`: discarding a set of
  variables has kernel spanned by those variables, identifying the quotient with the polynomial ring
  in the remaining variables.
* `MvPolynomial.ker_aeval_sumElim`: the graph equations generate the kernel of substitution
  which keeps the original variables.
* `MvPolynomial.ker_aeval_eq_comap_graph`: the relations among a family of polynomials are
  obtained by eliminating the original variables from its graph ideal.
* `MvPolynomial.sub_C_eval_mem_span_X_sub_C`, `MvPolynomial.ker_eval`,
  `MvPolynomial.isCoprime_ker_eval_iff`, `MvPolynomial.isCoprime_ker_eval_of_isUnit_sub`,
  `MvPolynomial.isCoprime_ker_eval`, `MvPolynomial.isCoprime_ker_eval_sq`,
  `MvPolynomial.mem_ker_eval_sup_map_C_iff` and `MvPolynomial.C_mem_sup_ker_eval_iff`: the kernel of
  point evaluation `eval a` is generated by the linear equations `X i - C (a i)`, two point
  ideals are comaximal iff the coordinate differences generate the unit ideal (covering unit
  differences and distinct points over a field), and modulo this kernel membership in `I · R[X]`
  or `H` reduces to evaluation at `a`.
* `Ideal.span_inf_span_eq_comap_rename_some`: an intersection of generated ideals is the
  contraction of an ideal in one more variable.
* `Ideal.mem_comap_rename_some_map_rename_some_sup_span_iff` and
  `Ideal.comap_rename_some_map_rename_some_sup_span`: the saturation of an ideal by a polynomial is
  the contraction of an ideal in one more variable, and the contraction from the localization.
* `Ideal.adjoin_range_quotient_mk_X_eq_top`: the residue classes of the variables generate any
  quotient `MvPolynomial σ R ⧸ I` as an `R`-algebra.

## References

* D. Cox, J. Little, D. O'Shea, *Ideals, Varieties, and Algorithms*, Chapter 4, §3,
  computing intersections by elimination; Chapter 4, §4, computing saturations by
  elimination; Chapter 3, §3, implicitization by elimination.
-/

public section

namespace MvPolynomial

open Finsupp

variable {R σ : Type*} [CommSemiring R]

variable (σ R) in
/-- The kernel of the constant coefficient is the ideal generated by the variables. -/
theorem ker_constantCoeff : RingHom.ker (constantCoeff (σ := σ) (R := R)) = idealOfVars σ R := by
  ext p
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker, ← pow_one (idealOfVars σ R), mem_pow_idealOfVars_iff', constantCoeff_eq]
  simp [degree_eq_zero_iff]

/-- Evaluating the ideal of the variables gives the ideal spanned by their values. -/
theorem map_aeval_idealOfVars {A : Type*} [CommSemiring A] [Algebra R A] (g : σ → A) :
    (idealOfVars σ R).map (aeval g) = Ideal.span (Set.range g) := by
  rw [idealOfVars, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  simp only [Function.comp_def, aeval_X]

/-- Evaluating the ideal of the variables along a ring homomorphism of the coefficients gives the
ideal spanned by the values of the variables. -/
theorem map_eval₂Hom_idealOfVars {A : Type*} [CommSemiring A] (c : R →+* A) (g : σ → A) :
    (idealOfVars σ R).map (eval₂Hom c g) = Ideal.span (Set.range g) := by
  rw [idealOfVars, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  simp only [Function.comp_def, coe_eval₂Hom, eval₂_X]

/-- A change of coefficients maps the `k`-th power of the ideal generated by the variables into the
`k`-th power of the ideal generated by the variables. -/
theorem pow_idealOfVars_le_comap_map {S : Type*} [CommSemiring S] (φ : R →+* S) (k : ℕ) :
    idealOfVars σ R ^ k ≤ (idealOfVars σ S ^ k).comap (map φ) := by
  intro p hp
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, mem_pow_idealOfVars_iff'] at *
  intro e he
  rw [coeff_map, hp e he, map_zero]

/-- Under coefficient reduction `MvPolynomial σ R →+* MvPolynomial σ (R ⧸ I)`, the preimage of
the monomial ideal generated by `X '' s` is `I.map C ⊔ Ideal.span (X '' s)`. -/
theorem comap_map_quotient_mk_span_X_image {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) (s : Set σ) :
    Ideal.comap (MvPolynomial.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) :
        MvPolynomial σ R →+* MvPolynomial σ (R ⧸ I)) (Ideal.span (X '' s)) =
      I.map C ⊔ Ideal.span (X '' s) := by
  let π : MvPolynomial σ R →+* MvPolynomial σ (R ⧸ I) := MvPolynomial.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)
  have hmap : Ideal.map π (Ideal.span (X '' s)) = Ideal.span (X '' s) := by
    simp [π, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_image]
  rw [← hmap, Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective π (map_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective),
    ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, ker_map, Ideal.mk_ker, sup_comm]

/-- Over a field, the ideal generated by all variables is maximal. -/
instance isMaximal_idealOfVars (σ K : Type*) [Field K] : (idealOfVars σ K).IsMaximal := by
  rw [← ker_constantCoeff]
  exact RingHom.ker_isMaximal_of_surjective (constantCoeff : MvPolynomial σ K →+* K)
    (fun scalar ↦ ⟨C scalar, by simp⟩)

/-- Over a nontrivial commutative semiring, a variable `X i` lies in the ideal generated by `X '' s`
if and only if `i ∈ s`. -/
@[simp]
theorem X_mem_ideal_span_X_image_iff [Nontrivial R] {s : Set σ} {i : σ} :
    (X i : MvPolynomial σ R) ∈ Ideal.span (X '' s) ↔ i ∈ s := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun hi ↦ Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨j, hj, hij⟩ := mem_ideal_span_X_image.mp h (Finsupp.single i 1) (by simp [support_X])
  have heq : i = j := by
    by_contra hne
    simp [hne] at hij
  exact heq ▸ hj

/-- If every variable has positive weight, any variable occurring in a weighted homogeneous
polynomial of weight `m` that lies in the square of the ideal of variables has weight strictly
less than `m`: every monomial in the support has total degree at least `2`. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.apply_lt_of_mem_sq_idealOfVars {w : σ → ℕ} (hw : ∀ j, 0 < w j)
    {m : ℕ} {q : MvPolynomial σ R} (hq : q.IsWeightedHomogeneous w m)
    (hq2 : q ∈ idealOfVars σ R ^ 2) {k : σ} (hk : k ∈ q.vars) : w k < m := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd, hdk⟩ := (mem_vars_iff_mem_support k).1 hk
  have hd_deg : 2 ≤ d.degree := (mem_pow_idealOfVars_iff 2 q).1 hq2 d hd
  have hd_wt : d.weight w = m := hq (mem_support_iff.1 hd)
  have hdk_ne : d k ≠ 0 := Finsupp.mem_support_iff.1 hdk
  have hsub_deg : (d - Finsupp.single k 1).degree + 1 = d.degree := by
    rw [Finsupp.degree_eq_weight_one]
    exact Finsupp.weight_sub_single_add (w := fun _ : σ ↦ 1) hdk_ne
  have hsub_ne : d - Finsupp.single k 1 ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    rw [h0, map_zero, zero_add] at hsub_deg
    omega
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := Finsupp.support_nonempty_iff.2 hsub_ne
  have hpos : 0 < (d - Finsupp.single k 1).weight w :=
    lt_of_lt_of_le (hw j)
      (Finsupp.le_weight_of_ne_zero (fun _ ↦ Nat.zero_le _) (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.1 hj))
  have hsub_wt := Finsupp.weight_sub_single_add (w := w) hdk_ne
  omega

/-- Over a nontrivial commutative semiring, the ideal generated by infinitely many variables is not
finitely generated: any finite set of polynomials involves only finitely many variables. -/
theorem not_fg_idealOfVars (σ R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] [Nontrivial R] [Infinite σ] :
    ¬ (idealOfVars σ R).FG := by
  classical
  rintro ⟨G, hG⟩
  let t : Finset σ := G.biUnion fun g ↦ g.support.biUnion Finsupp.support
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Infinite.exists_notMem_finset t
  have hle : idealOfVars σ R ≤ Ideal.span (X '' (t : Set σ)) := by
    rw [← hG, Ideal.span_le]
    intro g hg
    have hg' : g ∈ Ideal.span (X '' (Set.univ : Set σ)) := by
      rw [Set.image_univ, ← idealOfVars, ← hG]
      exact Ideal.subset_span hg
    refine mem_ideal_span_X_image.mpr fun m hm ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨j, -, hj⟩ := mem_ideal_span_X_image.mp hg' m hm
    exact ⟨j, Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨g, hg, Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr
      ⟨m, hm, Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr hj⟩⟩, hj⟩
  exact hi (X_mem_ideal_span_X_image_iff.mp (hle (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)))

/-- Over a nontrivial commutative semiring, the ideal generated by all variables is finitely
generated if and only if the index type is finite. -/
@[simp]
theorem fg_idealOfVars_iff [Nontrivial R] : (idealOfVars σ R).FG ↔ Finite σ :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ by
    by_contra hinf
    have := not_finite_iff_infinite.mp hinf
    exact not_fg_idealOfVars σ R h, fun _ ↦ fg_idealOfVars σ R⟩

/-- Over a nontrivial commutative semiring, a polynomial ring in infinitely many variables is not
noetherian, since its ideal of variables is not finitely generated. -/
theorem not_isNoetherianRing (σ R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] [Nontrivial R] [Infinite σ] :
    ¬ IsNoetherianRing (MvPolynomial σ R) :=
  fun h ↦ not_fg_idealOfVars σ R (h.noetherian _)

/-- If `p` lies in the `k`-th power of the ideal generated by the variables, then the coefficients
of `p * q` in total degree at most `k` are those of `p` times the constant coefficient of `q`. -/
theorem coeff_mul_of_mem_pow_idealOfVars (p : MvPolynomial σ R) {k : ℕ}
    (hp : p ∈ idealOfVars σ R ^ k) (q : MvPolynomial σ R) {e : σ →₀ ℕ} (he : degree e ≤ k) :
    (p * q).coeff e = p.coeff e * constantCoeff q := by
  classical
  rw [coeff_mul, Finset.sum_eq_single (e, 0), constantCoeff_eq]
  · rintro ⟨a, b⟩ hab hne
    rw [Finset.mem_antidiagonal] at hab
    have hb : degree b ≠ 0 := by
      rw [Ne, degree_eq_zero_iff]
      rintro rfl
      exact hne (by simp_all)
    have hdeg : degree a + degree b = degree e := by rw [← map_add, hab]
    rw [(mem_pow_idealOfVars_iff' k p).mp hp a (by omega), zero_mul]
  · exact fun h ↦ absurd (Finset.mem_antidiagonal.mpr (add_zero e)) h

/-- **Distinct lowest monomials are linearly independent.** Over a ring without zero divisors, a
family of polynomials is linearly independent if each member `v i` is a nonzero multiple of a
monomial `s i` up to terms of higher total degree, that is, modulo the `(degree (s i) + 1)`-th
power of the ideal of the variables, and the monomials `s i` are pairwise distinct. -/
theorem linearIndependent_of_sub_monomial_mem_pow_idealOfVars {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [NoZeroDivisors R] {ι : Type*} {v : ι → MvPolynomial σ R} {s : ι → σ →₀ ℕ}
    (hs : Function.Injective s) {c : ι → R} (hc : ∀ i, c i ≠ 0)
    (hv : ∀ i, v i - monomial (s i) (c i) ∈ idealOfVars σ R ^ (degree (s i) + 1)) :
    LinearIndependent R v := by
  classical
  -- In total degree at most that of `s j`, the only monomial of `v j` is `s j`.
  have hcoeff (i j : ι) (hij : degree (s i) ≤ degree (s j)) :
      (v j).coeff (s i) = if i = j then c j else 0 := by
    have h := (mem_pow_idealOfVars_iff' _ _).mp (hv j) (s i) (Nat.lt_succ_of_le hij)
    rw [AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_sub, Finsupp.sub_apply, coeff_monomial, sub_eq_zero] at h
    simp only [h, hs.eq_iff, eq_comm]
  rw [linearIndependent_iff']
  intro t g hg i hi
  -- Induct on the degree of `s i`: the coefficient of `s i` in the combination is `g i * c i`.
  induction hd : degree (s i) using Nat.strong_induction_on generalizing i with
  | _ d ih =>
    have h := congrArg (fun p : MvPolynomial σ R ↦ p.coeff (s i)) hg
    simp only [coeff_sum, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_smul_apply] at h
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single_of_mem i hi, hcoeff i i le_rfl] at h
    · simp only [↓reduceIte, smul_eq_mul] at h
      exact (mul_eq_zero.mp h).resolve_right (hc i)
    · intro j hj hji
      rcases lt_or_ge (degree (s j)) d with hlt | hle
      · rw [ih _ hlt j hj rfl, zero_smul]
      · simp [hcoeff i j (hd ▸ hle), Ne.symm hji]

section Graph

variable {ι : Type*} {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- The graph of a family of polynomials is cut out by the equations
`Y i - f i`: their ideal is the kernel of substitution, keeping the original variables. -/
theorem ker_aeval_sumElim (f : ι → MvPolynomial σ R) :
    RingHom.ker (aeval (Sum.elim X f)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ X (Sum.inr i) - rename Sum.inl (f i)) := by
  let J := Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ X (Sum.inr i) - rename Sum.inl (f i))
  let q := Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R J
  have hrel (i : ι) : q (X (Sum.inr i)) = q (rename Sum.inl (f i)) :=
    Ideal.Quotient.eq.mpr (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self i))
  have hcomp : (q.comp (rename Sum.inl)).comp (aeval (Sum.elim X f)) = q := by
    ext i
    cases i with
    | inl j => simp
    | inr j => simpa using (hrel j).symm
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · intro p hp
    have hp0 : aeval (Sum.elim X f) p = 0 := RingHom.mem_ker.mp hp
    have := DFunLike.congr_fun hcomp p
    simpa [hp0, q, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem] using this.symm
  · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    simp [RingHom.mem_ker, aeval_rename, aeval_X_left_apply]

/-- The relations among a family of polynomials are obtained by eliminating the original
variables from its graph equations. No finiteness or field hypothesis is needed. -/
theorem ker_aeval_eq_comap_graph (f : ι → MvPolynomial σ R) :
    RingHom.ker (aeval f) =
      (Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ X (Sum.inr i) - rename Sum.inl (f i))).comap
        (rename (R := R) Sum.inr) := by
  rw [← ker_aeval_sumElim]
  ext p
  simp [RingHom.mem_ker, aeval_rename]

end Graph

section KillCompl

variable {R σ τ : Type*} [CommSemiring R]

/-- Discarding the variables outside the range of an injective renaming `f : τ → σ` has kernel
spanned by those complementary variables. -/
theorem ker_killCompl {f : τ → σ} (hf : Function.Injective f) :
    RingHom.ker (killCompl (R := R) hf) = Ideal.span (X '' (Set.range f)ᶜ) := by
  classical
  have hcomp : (rename (R := R) f).comp (killCompl hf) =
      aeval (fun i ↦ if i ∈ ((Set.range f)ᶜ)ᶜ then X (R := R) i else 0) := by
    refine algHom_ext fun i ↦ ?_
    by_cases hi : i ∈ Set.range f
    · obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := hi
      rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, ← rename_X (f := f) j, killCompl_rename_app hf]
      simp
    · have h0 : killCompl (R := R) hf (X i) = 0 :=
        killCompl_monomial_eq_zero_of_notMem_range hf (s := Finsupp.single i 1) 1 (by simp) hi
      rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, h0, map_zero, aeval_X]
      simp [hi]
  rw [span_X_image_eq_ker_aeval_ite_mem]
  ext p
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker, RingHom.mem_ker, ← DFunLike.congr_fun hcomp p, AlgHom.comp_apply,
    ← map_zero (rename (R := R) f), (rename_injective f hf).eq_iff]

/-- Discarding the variables in a set `s` has kernel `Ideal.span (X '' s)`. -/
theorem ker_killCompl_subtype (s : Set σ) :
    RingHom.ker (killCompl (R := R) (Subtype.val_injective (p := (· ∉ s)))) =
      Ideal.span (X '' s) := by
  rw [ker_killCompl]
  congr 2
  ext x
  simp

end KillCompl

section QuotientSpanXImage

variable (R : Type*) [CommRing R] {σ : Type*} (s : Set σ)

/-- Quotienting `MvPolynomial σ R` by the ideal spanned by the variables in `s` gives the
polynomial ring in the remaining variables `{i : σ // i ∉ s}`. -/
noncomputable def quotientSpanXImageEquiv :
    (MvPolynomial σ R ⧸ Ideal.span ((X : σ → MvPolynomial σ R) '' s)) ≃ₐ[R]
      MvPolynomial {i : σ // i ∉ s} R :=
  (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R (ker_killCompl_subtype (R := R) s).symm).trans
    (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfRightInverse
      (f := killCompl (R := R) (Subtype.val_injective (p := (· ∉ s))))
      (g := rename Subtype.val)
      (killCompl_rename_app Subtype.val_injective))

variable {R s}

/-- On a representative polynomial, `quotientSpanXImageEquiv` discards the variables in `s`. -/
-- Not `@[simp]`: fails `simpNF` on `quotientSpanXImageEquiv_mk_X_of_notMem` (`killCompl` has no
-- `@[simp]` rule on `X i`) and breaks `AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply` on `Ideal.Quotient.mk _ p`.
theorem quotientSpanXImageEquiv_mk (p : MvPolynomial σ R) :
    quotientSpanXImageEquiv R s (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ p) =
      killCompl (Subtype.val_injective (p := (· ∉ s))) p :=
  (rfl)

/-- A variable outside `s` maps to the corresponding variable of the quotient polynomial ring. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSpanXImageEquiv_mk_X_of_notMem {i : σ} (hi : i ∉ s) :
    quotientSpanXImageEquiv R s (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X i)) = X ⟨i, hi⟩ := by
  let j : {k : σ // k ∉ s} := ⟨i, hi⟩
  rw [quotientSpanXImageEquiv_mk, ← rename_X (f := Subtype.val) j]
  exact killCompl_rename_app (Subtype.val_injective (p := (· ∉ s))) (X j)

/-- A variable in `s` maps to zero in the quotient polynomial ring. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSpanXImageEquiv_mk_X_of_mem {i : σ} (hi : i ∈ s) :
    quotientSpanXImageEquiv R s (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X i)) = 0 := by
  rw [quotientSpanXImageEquiv_mk]
  exact killCompl_monomial_eq_zero_of_notMem_range Subtype.val_injective
    (s := Finsupp.single i 1) 1 (a := i) (by simp) (by rintro ⟨⟨_, hj⟩, rfl⟩; exact hj hi)

/-- The inverse of `quotientSpanXImageEquiv` embeds polynomials in the remaining variables via
`rename Subtype.val` and projects to the quotient. -/
-- Not `@[simp]`: fails `simpNF` on `quotientSpanXImageEquiv_symm_X` and breaks
-- `AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply` under `simp`.
theorem quotientSpanXImageEquiv_symm_apply (q : MvPolynomial {i : σ // i ∉ s} R) :
    (quotientSpanXImageEquiv R s).symm q = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (rename Subtype.val q) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The inverse of `quotientSpanXImageEquiv` sends each variable `X i` (`i ∉ s`) to the class of
`X i.1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSpanXImageEquiv_symm_X (i : {i : σ // i ∉ s}) :
    (quotientSpanXImageEquiv R s).symm (X i) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X i.val) := by
  simp [quotientSpanXImageEquiv_symm_apply]

end QuotientSpanXImage

section PointEvaluation

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- Every multivariate polynomial differs from its value at `a` by an element of the ideal
generated by `X i - C (a i)`. -/
theorem sub_C_eval_mem_span_X_sub_C (a : σ → R) (p : MvPolynomial σ R) :
    p - C (eval a p) ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : σ ↦ X i - C (a i)) := by
  let J : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ R) := Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : σ ↦ X i - C (a i))
  let q : MvPolynomial σ R →+* MvPolynomial σ R ⧸ J := Ideal.Quotient.mk J
  have hcomp : (q.comp (C (σ := σ))).comp (eval a) = q := by
    refine ringHom_ext' (by ext r; simp) fun i ↦ ?_
    simp only [RingHom.comp_apply, eval_X, q]
    symm
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq.mpr (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)
  have hp := RingHom.congr_fun hcomp p
  simp only [RingHom.comp_apply, q] at hp
  exact Ideal.Quotient.eq.mp hp.symm

/-- The kernel of point evaluation `eval a` is generated by the linear equations `X i - C (a i)`.
No finiteness or field hypothesis is needed. -/
theorem ker_eval (a : σ → R) :
    RingHom.ker (eval a) = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : σ ↦ X i - C (a i)) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun p hp ↦ ?_) (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · have hp0 : eval a p = 0 := RingHom.mem_ker.mp hp
    simpa only [hp0, map_zero, sub_zero] using sub_C_eval_mem_span_X_sub_C a p
  · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    simp [RingHom.mem_ker]

/-- A polynomial belongs to `ker (eval a) + I · R[X]` if and only if its value at `a` lies in
`I`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_ker_eval_sup_map_C_iff (a : σ → R) (I : Ideal R) (p : MvPolynomial σ R) :
    p ∈ RingHom.ker (eval a) ⊔ I.map (C (σ := σ)) ↔ eval a p ∈ I := by
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (eval a) := fun r ↦ ⟨C r, eval_C r⟩
  have hcomp : (eval a).comp (C (σ := σ)) = RingHom.id R := by ext; simp
  rw [sup_comm, RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, ← Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective (eval a) hsurj,
    Ideal.map_map, hcomp, Ideal.map_id, Ideal.mem_comap]

/-- A constant `C r` belongs to `H + ker (eval a)` if and only if `r` belongs to the image of `H`
under `eval a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem C_mem_sup_ker_eval_iff (a : σ → R) (H : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ R)) (r : R) :
    C r ∈ H ⊔ RingHom.ker (eval a) ↔ r ∈ H.map (eval a) := by
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (eval a) := fun s ↦ ⟨C s, eval_C s⟩
  rw [RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, ← Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective (eval a) hsurj,
    Ideal.mem_comap, eval_C]

/-- Two evaluation ideals `ker (eval P)` and `ker (eval Q)` are comaximal if and only if the
coordinate differences `P j - Q j` generate the unit ideal. -/
theorem isCoprime_ker_eval_iff {P Q : σ → R} :
    IsCoprime (RingHom.ker (eval P)) (RingHom.ker (eval Q)) ↔
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ P j - Q j) = ⊤ := by
  rw [Ideal.isCoprime_iff_sup_eq]
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ (Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).2 ?_, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  · have hmap : (RingHom.ker (eval P) ⊔ RingHom.ker (eval Q)).map (eval Q) ≤
        Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ P j - Q j) := by
      rw [Ideal.map_sup, RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot (eval Q),
        Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _ fun r ↦ ⟨C r, eval_C r⟩, sup_bot_eq, ker_eval,
        Ideal.map_span, Ideal.span_le]
      rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨j, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      have hmem : -(P j - Q j) ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ P j - Q j) :=
        neg_mem (Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩)
      simpa only [map_sub, eval_X, eval_C, neg_sub] using SetLike.mem_coe.2 hmem
    exact hmap (h ▸ by simpa using
      Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (eval Q) (Submodule.mem_top (x := (1 : MvPolynomial σ R))))
  · refine top_le_iff.1 ?_
    rw [← Ideal.map_top (C (σ := σ)), ← h, Ideal.map_span, Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨j, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    have hsub : C (P j - Q j) = (X j - C (Q j)) - (X j - C (P j)) := by
      rw [map_sub]; ring
    rw [hsub]
    exact sub_mem (Ideal.mem_sup_right (by simp [RingHom.mem_ker]))
      (Ideal.mem_sup_left (by simp [RingHom.mem_ker]))

/-- If two points `P, Q : σ → R` differ by a unit in some coordinate, their evaluation ideals are
comaximal. -/
theorem isCoprime_ker_eval_of_isUnit_sub {P Q : σ → R} {j : σ} (h : IsUnit (P j - Q j)) :
    IsCoprime (RingHom.ker (eval P)) (RingHom.ker (eval Q)) :=
  isCoprime_ker_eval_iff.2 (Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩) h)

/-- Over a field, the ideals of two distinct points are coprime. -/
theorem isCoprime_ker_eval {k : Type*} [Field k] {P Q : σ → k} (h : P ≠ Q) :
    IsCoprime (RingHom.ker (eval P)) (RingHom.ker (eval Q)) := by
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := Function.ne_iff.1 h
  exact isCoprime_ker_eval_of_isUnit_sub (isUnit_iff_ne_zero.2 (sub_ne_zero.2 hj))

/-- Over a field, the squares of the ideals of two distinct points are coprime. -/
theorem isCoprime_ker_eval_sq {k : Type*} [Field k] {P Q : σ → k} (h : P ≠ Q) :
    IsCoprime (RingHom.ker (eval P) ^ 2) (RingHom.ker (eval Q) ^ 2) :=
  (isCoprime_ker_eval h).pow

end PointEvaluation

end MvPolynomial

namespace Ideal

open MvPolynomial

variable {σ R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- An ideal intersection is the contraction of the ideal generated by the two families
multiplied by the auxiliary variable and its complement. -/
theorem span_inf_span_eq_comap_rename_some (s t : Set (MvPolynomial σ R)) :
    span s ⊓ span t =
      (span ((fun f ↦ X none * rename some f) '' s ∪
        (fun g ↦ (1 - X none) * rename some g) '' t)).comap
          (rename (R := R) some) := by
  let e := (optionEquivLeft R σ).toRingHom
  let K : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Option σ) R) :=
    span ((fun f ↦ X none * rename some f) '' s ∪
      (fun g ↦ (1 - X none) * rename some g) '' t)
  have hcomp : e.comp (rename (R := R) some).toRingHom = Polynomial.C := by
    ext <;> simp [e]
  have hmap : K.map e =
      span ((fun f ↦ Polynomial.X * Polynomial.C f) '' s ∪
        (fun g ↦ (1 - Polynomial.X) * Polynomial.C g) '' t) := by
    have he (f : MvPolynomial σ R) : e (rename some f) = Polynomial.C f :=
      RingHom.congr_fun hcomp f
    have hX : e (X none) = Polynomial.X := optionEquivLeft_X_none R σ
    simp only [K, map_span, Set.image_union, Set.image_image, map_mul, map_sub, map_one, he, hX]
  rw [span_inf_span_eq_comap_C, ← hmap, ← hcomp, ← comap_comap,
    K.comap_map_of_bijective e (optionEquivLeft R σ).bijective,
    AlgHom.toRingHom_eq_coe, comap_coe]

/-- **Saturation by an added variable.** A polynomial `g` lies in the contraction along
`rename some` of `I + (f X_none - 1)` if and only if some power of `f` multiplies it into `I`. -/
theorem mem_comap_rename_some_map_rename_some_sup_span_iff {I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ R)}
    {f g : MvPolynomial σ R} :
    g ∈ (I.map (rename some) ⊔ span {rename some f * X none - 1}).comap
      (rename (R := R) some) ↔ ∃ n : ℕ, f ^ n * g ∈ I := by
  -- Transport to polynomials in `X none` over `MvPolynomial σ R`, where `rename some` is `C`.
  let e := (optionEquivLeft R σ).toAlgHom
  have hcomp : e.comp (rename (R := R) some) = Polynomial.CAlgHom := by
    ext; simp [e]
  have hf : e (rename some f) = Polynomial.C f := AlgHom.congr_fun hcomp f
  have hX : e (X none) = Polynomial.X := optionEquivLeft_X_none R σ
  have hmap : (I.map (rename some) ⊔ span {rename some f * X none - 1}).map e =
      I.map (Polynomial.CAlgHom (R := R)) ⊔ span {Polynomial.C f * Polynomial.X - 1} := by
    simp [map_sup, map_mapₐ, map_span, hcomp, hf, hX]
  rw [← comap_map_of_bijective e (optionEquivLeft R σ).bijective (I := I.map (rename some) ⊔ _),
    hmap, comap_comapₐ, hcomp]
  exact mem_comap_C_map_C_sup_span_C_mul_X_sub_one_iff

/-- The contraction along `rename some` of `I + (f X_none - 1)` is the contraction of `I` from
the localization `S` of `MvPolynomial σ R` away from `f`. -/
theorem comap_rename_some_map_rename_some_sup_span (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ R))
    (f : MvPolynomial σ R) (S : Type*) [CommSemiring S] [Algebra (MvPolynomial σ R) S]
    [IsLocalization.Away f S] :
    (I.map (rename some) ⊔ span {rename some f * X none - 1}).comap (rename (R := R) some) =
      (I.map (algebraMap _ S)).comap (algebraMap _ S) := by
  ext g
  rw [mem_comap_rename_some_map_rename_some_sup_span_iff, mem_comap,
    IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_mem_map_algebraMap_iff f]

/-- The quotient `MvPolynomial σ R ⧸ I` is generated as an `R`-algebra by the residue classes of the
variables `X i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem adjoin_range_quotient_mk_X_eq_top (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ R)) :
    Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range fun i : σ ↦ Quotient.mk I (X i)) = ⊤ := by
  rw [Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval, ← mkₐ_eq_aeval, AlgHom.range_eq_top]
  exact Quotient.mk_surjective

end Ideal
